(3055525, 425997, 45475, '<td valign="top">Yeah... nice to see another Pentax user in the top 10 ;) Those fast 50s are great, aren''t they? Awesome work on the DoF and huge congrats for the great finish!</td>', 'Yeah... nice to see another Pentax user in the top 10 ;) Those fast 50s are great, aren''t they? Awesome work on the DoF and huge congrats for the great finish!', '2006-11-22 16:56:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(3055528, 427335, 45475, '<td valign="top">Great work Chele! Congratulations!</td>', 'Great work Chele! Congratulations!', '2006-11-22 16:57:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(3055537, 427319, 45475, '<td valign="top">She must be a wonderfully patient creature to have let you do that to her! I thought this was a marvellous take on the challenge. Very creative :) Cheers and congrats for 7th place!!</td>', 'She must be a wonderfully patient creature to have let you do that to her! I thought this was a marvellous take on the challenge. Very creative :) Cheers and congrats for 7th place!!', '2006-11-22 17:00:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(3055568, 425693, 45475, '<td valign="top">I thought your timing was impeccable! A second later and the girl (who kinda mirrors the poster btw) would have blocked the hand and the comp wouldn''t have been nearly as good. Way to go, congrats on your top 20 finish!</td>', 'I thought your timing was impeccable! A second later and the girl (who kinda mirrors the poster btw) would have blocked the hand and the comp wouldn''t have been nearly as good. Way to go, congrats on your top 20 finish!', '2006-11-22 17:11:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(3055635, 426028, 67189, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the feedback.<br/> <br/>I have got a lot to learn about light. I was trying so hard to soften the light but I could not get it. I was useing an old smith victor flood with an opus umbrella and stand. You can see the umbrella reflection in the bottom axe on the helmet. But it was a start. I found a some good info in the fourms about useing old nikon SB24''s or 25''s. So now I am on the hunt for them and with some practice I hope to get better.</td>', 'Thanks for the feedback. I have got a lot to learn about light. I was trying so hard to soften the light but I could not get it. I was useing an old smith victor flood with an opus umbrella and stand. You can see the umbrella reflection in the bottom axe on the helmet. But it was a start. I found a some good info in the fourms about useing old nikon SB24''s or 25''s. So now I am on the hunt for them and with some practice I hope to get better.', '2006-11-22 17:29:39.000000', NULL, 0),
