(3057330, 426156, 66923, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by eyewave:</b></div><hr/><i>  lot of voter don''t like any borders). <br/>Borders are important and help make a point or focus on the subject better. If they do not like it, thats their problem.<br/> <br/> Also, the crop might have been less close, I had preferred to see the hole stamp (why not make it a portrait format with a decent angle of the subject). </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I have a larger view, of course, just felt this crop matched the challenge better, since one could see the crown and the subject better. The subject was not the stamp, but the queen. Thanks for taking a look!</td>', 'Originally posted by eyewave:  lot of voter don''t like any borders). Borders are important and help make a point or focus on the subject better. If they do not like it, thats their problem.  Also, the crop might have been less close, I had preferred to see the hole stamp (why not make it a portrait format with a decent angle of the subject).   I have a larger view, of course, just felt this crop matched the challenge better, since one could see the crown and the subject better. The subject was not the stamp, but the queen. Thanks for taking a look!', '2006-11-23 09:56:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(3057562, 427594, 31443, '<td valign="top">Nice one Rebecca! I really liked this one during the challenge, what a nice lighting..</td>', 'Nice one Rebecca! I really liked this one during the challenge, what a nice lighting..', '2006-11-23 12:29:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(3057862, 427373, 18868, '<td valign="top">Hey there y''all... Thanks for the nice comments!<br/> <br/>I was trying to capture some of the nice fall colors and blue sky in the background, but the ones that had a nice background wound up with a blurry subject, or worse, a strange expression on my face.  This is technically a self-portrait.<br/> <br/>To answer the questions regarding how I achieved the blur within the rules of basic editing, I stood in front of several trees with nice colors, and held the camera out at arms length.  10-22mm lens at 10, and the apeture set to be pretty small, f18, in order to drive up the shutter speed, which was 1/5th of a second.  The natural light versions were too blurry to use, so I fired the built-in flash to get a crisp subject, yet allow the background to swirl.  <br/> <br/>One nice thing about the XTi with the 10mp capture is that it allowed me to dramatically crop the image down from the catpure and still get a very useable size.</td>', 'Hey there y''all... Thanks for the nice comments! I was trying to capture some of the nice fall colors and blue sky in the background, but the ones that had a nice background wound up with a blurry subject, or worse, a strange expression on my face.  This is technically a self-portrait. To answer the questions regarding how I achieved the blur within the rules of basic editing, I stood in front of several trees with nice colors, and held the camera out at arms length.  10-22mm lens at 10, and the apeture set to be pretty small, f18, in order to drive up the shutter speed, which was 1/5th of a second.  The natural light versions were too blurry to use, so I fired the built-in flash to get a crisp subject, yet allow the background to swirl.   One nice thing about the XTi with the 10mp capture is that it allowed me to dramatically crop the image down from the catpure and still get a very useable size.', '2006-11-23 14:42:00.000000', NULL, 0),
