(3068386, 425925, 24499, '<td valign="top">That''s the only angle that I wanted to see of my DI''s.  Even then, you somehow knew that they could see every mistake that you were even thinking about making.<br/> <br/>The campaign cover is the only piece of headgear in the world that puts a knot in the stomach of every Marine, even 40 years later.</td>', 'That''s the only angle that I wanted to see of my DI''s.  Even then, you somehow knew that they could see every mistake that you were even thinking about making. The campaign cover is the only piece of headgear in the world that puts a knot in the stomach of every Marine, even 40 years later.', '2006-11-28 13:51:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(3068594, 427549, 66193, '<td valign="top">marie, I have a comment, but it has nothing to do with the portrait technically (which I think is done quite nicely).  If i had been voting on this image, I wouldn''t have given it a high score because the emphasis of the capture appears to be a portrait of your husband.  There''s not enough emphasis on the headwear!  it kind of blends into the background.  When I vote in a challenge, I''ll make a first pass very quickly, looking for the extremes.  The image is only on my screen for a short time, and it must speak to me in those seconds.  My highest scores go to the images that make me spend some time giving it a long look.  Something catchy (composition, lighting, subject, humor, etc).  A minor technical detail such as a slightly blown highlight might stop you from getting a 10, but it won''t make it a 5!  just my 2 cents.  steve</td>', 'marie, I have a comment, but it has nothing to do with the portrait technically (which I think is done quite nicely).  If i had been voting on this image, I wouldn''t have given it a high score because the emphasis of the capture appears to be a portrait of your husband.  There''s not enough emphasis on the headwear!  it kind of blends into the background.  When I vote in a challenge, I''ll make a first pass very quickly, looking for the extremes.  The image is only on my screen for a short time, and it must speak to me in those seconds.  My highest scores go to the images that make me spend some time giving it a long look.  Something catchy (composition, lighting, subject, humor, etc).  A minor technical detail such as a slightly blown highlight might stop you from getting a 10, but it won''t make it a 5!  just my 2 cents.  steve', '2006-11-28 15:54:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(3068624, 427602, 69197, '<td valign="top">It''s lovely!  Really!<br/> <br/>Emily*<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-11-28 16:07:43.</i></td>', 'It''s lovely!  Really! Emily*', '2006-11-28 16:06:49.000000', '2006-11-28 16:07:43.000000', 0),
(3068962, 427497, 68279, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments folks.<br/> <br/>I intended it to be dim, but after looking at the comments I moved the image off my laptop and looked at it at work, and it''s MUCH darker.  It lost way too much definition.  I''m gonna have to go dig my monitor out of storage, the laptop display is simply too bright to give a realistic representation.<br/> <br/>Kerm, you''re right on target.  I thought I had a couple more days to play around with ideas, happened to glance at the site and found I only had a few hours, and of course I already had plans that night. So, this was totally rushed.<br/> <br/>Thanks for taking the time to leave some feedback.<br/> <br/>Brian<br/> <br/></td>', 'Thanks for the comments folks. I intended it to be dim, but after looking at the comments I moved the image off my laptop and looked at it at work, and it''s MUCH darker.  It lost way too much definition.  I''m gonna have to go dig my monitor out of storage, the laptop display is simply too bright to give a realistic representation. Kerm, you''re right on target.  I thought I had a couple more days to play around with ideas, happened to glance at the site and found I only had a few hours, and of course I already had plans that night. So, this was totally rushed. Thanks for taking the time to leave some feedback. Brian ', '2006-11-28 18:36:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(3069304, 427371, 51802, '<td valign="top"><b>Hello from the Critique Club!</b> <br/> <br/>I''m not much of a fan of high key shots, but this one works well and does not strike me as blown out.  The black and white is well done and is complemented by the grain in this pic.<br/> <br/>Being shot at 1/5 sec and ISO 800, this must have been done in fairly low light.  Good job on your exposure control!  <br/> <br/>Your use of the blinds as negative space really works well.  The grain of the photo looks very natural over what I am assuming are wood blinds.  This really helps keep the grain from being overpowering and helps set a solemn mood. <br/> <br/>Congrats on your top scoring photo so far!</td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club!  I''m not much of a fan of high key shots, but this one works well and does not strike me as blown out.  The black and white is well done and is complemented by the grain in this pic. Being shot at 1/5 sec and ISO 800, this must have been done in fairly low light.  Good job on your exposure control!   Your use of the blinds as negative space really works well.  The grain of the photo looks very natural over what I am assuming are wood blinds.  This really helps keep the grain from being overpowering and helps set a solemn mood.  Congrats on your top scoring photo so far!', '2006-11-28 21:31:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(3069350, 426134, 51802, '<td valign="top"><b>Hello from the Critique Club!</b> <br/> <br/>My first impression is very positive.  This is a very dramatic shot on several levels.  The lighting is what makes this shot.  Keeping her face in shadows works very well with the cold hard background.  Her pose, and having her hands bound as well as the stark background, all drive home the feeling of imprisonment. <br/> <br/>The soft focus is probably what kept you from scoring higher.  I really feel it fits this photo very well, but the general mentality of a DPC voter wants to see the subject in very sharp focus.<br/> <br/>Welcome to DPC!  You have done quite well for your first challenge entry and I look forward to seeing more of your work in the future!</td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club!  My first impression is very positive.  This is a very dramatic shot on several levels.  The lighting is what makes this shot.  Keeping her face in shadows works very well with the cold hard background.  Her pose, and having her hands bound as well as the stark background, all drive home the feeling of imprisonment.  The soft focus is probably what kept you from scoring higher.  I really feel it fits this photo very well, but the general mentality of a DPC voter wants to see the subject in very sharp focus. Welcome to DPC!  You have done quite well for your first challenge entry and I look forward to seeing more of your work in the future!', '2006-11-28 21:52:17.000000', NULL, 0),
