(3086415, 427303, 51538, '<td valign="top">If the flash in the shade had blasted off, then the ''short-circuit look'' would have been perceivable.  It needed that electrical flash which you could only get via the slave unit or by using fireworks.. ;-)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-12-04 12:07:17.</i></td>', 'If the flash in the shade had blasted off, then the ''short-circuit look'' would have been perceivable.  It needed that electrical flash which you could only get via the slave unit or by using fireworks.. ;-)', '2006-12-04 12:06:42.000000', '2006-12-04 12:07:17.000000', 0),
(3088759, 425785, 66201, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments. I learned a lot about considering background in this one. I had two of these guys actually and was trying to get a shot of them face to face, but the one that could have worked, had a dreadful background so I had to settle with this one.</td>', 'Thanks for the comments. I learned a lot about considering background in this one. I had two of these guys actually and was trying to get a shot of them face to face, but the one that could have worked, had a dreadful background so I had to settle with this one.', '2006-12-05 10:12:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(3115951, 427496, 16106, '<td valign="top">The angle and strength of the lighting brings up the texture of the hat very well, but a bit of bounce lighting on the otherside of the flash would have given the dark side of the hat a bit more interest, where it fades too much into black and the light punches through to make that interesting pattern. <br/> <br/>The hat is the star here, the headset doesn''t realy add much or go with this very country/folksy hat, and while the table cloth is beautiful, it seems a bit too soft and delicate for the hard pattens set up in the hat.<br/> <br/>The inky shadows on the hat where here ought to be some detail, and the slightly blown highlights on the table cloth make me wonder if you didn''t dial up the contrast a bit higher than needed to.</td>', 'The angle and strength of the lighting brings up the texture of the hat very well, but a bit of bounce lighting on the otherside of the flash would have given the dark side of the hat a bit more interest, where it fades too much into black and the light punches through to make that interesting pattern.  The hat is the star here, the headset doesn''t realy add much or go with this very country/folksy hat, and while the table cloth is beautiful, it seems a bit too soft and delicate for the hard pattens set up in the hat. The inky shadows on the hat where here ought to be some detail, and the slightly blown highlights on the table cloth make me wonder if you didn''t dial up the contrast a bit higher than needed to.', '2006-12-14 00:30:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(3117804, 425693, 41337, '<td valign="top">Quirky indeed. I love the tones in this.</td>', 'Quirky indeed. I love the tones in this.', '2006-12-14 16:16:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(3118928, 427496, 36988, '<td valign="top">Have to be a bit carefull when shooting a pattern such as what''s in the hat. Although I''m sure it looks great on some monitors, it can also look overly sharpened as is the case on mine. I''ve got a very high contrast and very sharp monitor, as do many folks here and it''s hard to strike a ballance that will match all conditions.<br/>Might have tried a nore gradual transition between the light and shadow on the hat as well as it drops to almost black very suddenly and can be a bit startling.<br/>Otherwise I like the image and think with a little refinement, it could be quite exceptional... :)</td>', 'Have to be a bit carefull when shooting a pattern such as what''s in the hat. Although I''m sure it looks great on some monitors, it can also look overly sharpened as is the case on mine. I''ve got a very high contrast and very sharp monitor, as do many folks here and it''s hard to strike a ballance that will match all conditions.Might have tried a nore gradual transition between the light and shadow on the hat as well as it drops to almost black very suddenly and can be a bit startling.Otherwise I like the image and think with a little refinement, it could be quite exceptional... :)', '2006-12-14 23:57:20.000000', NULL, 0),
